Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 21:58:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/21] Session metadata column
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a JSON-typed `metadata` column to the `session` table so callers
can attach structured attribution to each session. Round-trips
through `Session.create({metadata: {...}})`, `Session.get(id).metadata`,
and the SDK's create/get types.

Used by the hivemind memory-compaction daemon to record
`triggered_by_session`, `target_agent`, and `triggered_at_bytes` on
each spawn — so observers (TUI session tree, MCP `list_sessions`,
future tooling) can see why a session exists without parsing its
title.

  - session.sql.ts: `metadata: text({mode: "json"}).$type<...>()`
  - migration/20260507120000_session_metadata/migration.sql:
      ALTER TABLE `session` ADD `metadata` text;
  - session/index.ts: `Info.metadata` zod schema; `createNext` and
      `create` accept `metadata?: Record<string, unknown>`.
  - projectors.ts: pass-through in `toPartialRow`; `fromRow`/`toRow`
      already covered by the schema reflection.
  - test/session/metadata.test.ts: round-trip, default-undefined,
      nested-values.
